    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***UNDER OFFER***\r\n\r\nDiscover the ultimate in village convenience and eco-friendly living with this charming 3-bedroom end-of-terrace home, perfectly situated on Main Street, Ballylongford. Combining a highly desirable central village location with a warm, inviting atmosphere, this cozy dwelling allows you to leave the car behind and walk to everything the community has to offer. Local shops, the primary school, the church, a vibrant playground, and traditional pubs are all just steps from your front door.  Featuring reliable oil-fired central heating alongside energy-saving solar panels, this property boasts a B energy rating which may qualify potential purchasers for a green mortgage.   Inside, the home offers a wonderfully charming and cozy layout, ideal for creating a peaceful retreat from the outside world. To the rear, you will find a fully enclosed, private courtyard—a low-maintenance outdoor space perfect for relaxing, container gardening, or hosting intimate gatherings in complete privacy.  \r\n\r\nBeyond the village, commuter convenience is unparalleled. Positioned right on the pulse of North Kerry, the property boasts easy accessibility to Tarbert, the seaside resort of Ballybunion, and the heritage town of Listowel, while also connecting seamlessly to Limerick city. Furthermore, its close proximity to the Tarbert Ferry opens up effortless access across the Shannon estuary to County Clare and the scenic Wild Atlantic Way. This property represents a fantastic, turn-key opportunity for first-time buyers, investors, or holiday home hunters seeking a comfortable base with unbeatable amenities right on their doorstep."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 6.15m x 1.77m \r\nTiled and wood flooring, open string staircase to first floor. Storage space under stairs.  \r\n\r\nLiving Room - 2.8m x 4.7m \r\nWood flooring, solid fuel stove on raised tiled hearth - streetside view.\r\n\r\nKitchen - 2.9m x 5.2m \r\nWood flooring, fitted kitchen with electric oven, gas hob and extractor fan - large feature window overlooking courtyard. \r\n\r\nRear Lobby & WC - 3.9m x 1.6m \r\nWood flooring, French doors leading to decking and courtyard.  Downstairs toilet - tiled floor to ceiling, wc, whb and frosted window.\r\n\r\nLanding - 2.3m x 2.9m \r\nWood flooring, access to attic via Stira - window overlooking rear courtyard.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 2.8m x 2.8m \r\nWood flooring - overlooking Main Street. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 3.6m x 2.8m \r\nWood flooring - overlooking Main Street.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 3.4m x 2.6m \r\nWood flooring and hot-press - overlooking rear courtyard.\r\n\r\nBathroom - 1.9m x 2.2m \r\nTiled floor to ceiling, wc, whb, corner bath with overhead Triton thermostatic power shower (AS2000xt), heated towel rail and frosted window.\r\n\r\nLock-up Store - 2.3m x 3.2m \r\nBlock built with slate roof, plumbed for washer/dryer - contains oil tank.\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Located in the heart of Ballylongford village.\r\nProximity to Beale, Ballybunion and Littor beach.\r\nReady for immediate occupation\r\nOil fired central heating.\r\nSolar panels front & back (hot water only).\r\nDouble glazed PVC windows & doors\r\nAll mains services"
      },
